Subject: [PATCH] Preserve unaffected SSL.com TLS trust without the AAA root

Trust the self-signed SSL.com TLS ECC Root CA 2022 directly so that
unaffected SSL.com chains do not depend on the removed AAA cross-sign.
This root is already trusted for TLS in Azure Linux's Microsoft CA data.
Keep the incident-related AAA and emSign ECC G3 roots removed.

Source: https://repo-certs.ssl.com/repo/certs/SSLcom-TLS-Root-2022-ECC.pem
SHA-256: c32ffd9f46f936d16c3673990959434b9ad60aafbb9e7cf33654f144cc1ba143
Upstream-status: Azure Linux trust-store backport

--- a/etc/roots.pem
+++ b/etc/roots.pem
@@ -4297,3 +4297,20 @@
 SaSS6sUUiHCm0w2wqsosQJz76YJumgIwK0eaB8bRwoF8yguWGEEbo/QwCZ61IygN
 nxS2PFOiTAZpffpskcYqSUXm7LcT4Tps
 -----END CERTIFICATE-----
